  "solution": {
    "text": "The equation of the curve is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br />The curve is symmetrical about the <math> <mtext>y</mtext> </math>-axis.<br /><br />Also, it is a polynomial of degree four having roots <math> <mrow> <mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo>±</mo><mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>2</mn> </msqrt> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>.</mo></mrow></math><br /><br /><math><mtext>x</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn> </math> is repeated root. Hence, graph touches <math> <mtext>x</mtext> </math> -axis at <math> <mrow> <mtext>(0,0)</mtext></mrow> </math> and intersects the <math> <mtext>x</mtext> </math> -axis at <math> <mrow> <mtext>A</mtext><mfenced> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>2</mn> </msqrt> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>0</mn></mrow> </mfenced><mtext> </mtext><mo>&amp;</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext>B</mtext><mfenced> <mrow> <mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>2</mn> </msqrt> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>0</mn></mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>⇒</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>dy</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <mtext>dx</mtext></mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msup> <mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>x</mtext></mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>x</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext>x</mtext><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mfenced> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>d</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mtext>y</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <mtext>d</mtext><msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow> </math> at <math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> and at <math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br />So x = <math> <mrow> <mo>±</mo><mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> are the points of local minima<br /><br />Thus, the graph of the curve is shown in diagram.<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/dnfedmgwlckyrduhidcbjcayypczokljumeqalhzzftelkjkkk.jpeg\" /><br /><br />Here, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></math> , as <math> <mtext>x</mtext> </math> varies from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo></math> The required area<br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"false\">∫</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"false\">∫</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></munderover><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>120</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
